  "loc.src.data.kettleline.field.body.4d1003ffc5ef": "Rib clusters and pod frames sheared inward, against the convoy\\u2019s own run.",
  "loc.src.data.kettleline.field.body.58a9cf9378be": "The Kettle Line\\u2019s drive stern, its bell slagged from the inside: the engineers",
  "loc.src.data.kettleline.field.body.8ff2e7dbcaa2": "A loaded piece of the Kettle Line, torn loose right off the gate approach with its",
  "loc.src.data.kettleline.field.name.425b2cd33bb2": "Kettle Line Stern",
  "loc.src.data.kettleline.field.name.8c280f9c5685": "Kettle Line Shard",
  "loc.src.data.kettleline.field.name.adc9635bbd8c": "Kettle Line pay strongbox",
  "loc.src.data.kettleline.field.name.b0dd31a25526": "Kettle Line Ribs",
  "loc.src.data.kettleline.field.title.1c8c494f71c9": "Kettle Line — the Stern That Refused",
  "loc.src.data.kettleline.field.title.2d79bb87447e": "Kettle Line — First Overboard",
  "loc.src.data.kettleline.field.title.548c517e15b9": "Kettle Line — Sheared Ribs",
  "loc.src.data.kettleline.field.title.6f2d01a8dd93": "The Kettle Line",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.body.04d31318726b": "Seventeen intact freighters, seventeen living-crew counts from zero to sixteen, every bunk warm, no transmitter answering by name. The buoy counts seventeen.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.body.0adccdee59ba": "One amber-lit wall continues below the drilled cavity. The snapped auger tooth in the foreground is folded, not worn. No scale or telemetry survived the return.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.body.1a865220cfdf": "The close pass crosses a dry river basin and one street of the dead city lights beneath it, briefly, while the reader holds inside the shadow. The batteries answer after eighty million years — slowly, like something waking.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.body.60729d53be76": "The close pass returns three readable registries — a mule line-hauler, a Vael cutter, a drifter nobody claimed — and one plate that answers no registry at all. It is newer than the wall around it, and welded blank on purpose.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.body.72294393f2a1": "Four shard-notes align into a phrase that ends before its answer. The shrine identifies the silence as part of the composition: the Vael schism removed a voice, not merely a faction.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.body.7cafed27627e": "A close reading resolves the Obelisk into intervals rather than a message. The next pulse is shorter than the last; the gaps are the only part that remains still.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.body.97d64ab075a3": "One full cycle from under the beam: 8.00 seconds, except the eighth, which runs short by a fixed hair. The gap has been narrowing on every recorded pass. Quiet's crossing logs cluster inside it.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.brief.343d4680d77e": "Return to the Obelisk and take one close reading. Every extra pulse brings the Vael watch forward.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.brief.3eb06da439da": "Bring the reader inside the arc's shadow and fire one close scanner pulse across the interior face.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.brief.5e2e4211260d": "Return to the shaft and fire one close scanner pulse to drop the hardened probe.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.brief.6a3df54adc9a": "Hold close along the fortress wall and fire one scanner pass deep enough to read the welded plate registries.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.brief.8b272f7ed884": "Return to the sphere and fire one close scanner pulse while the Echo Shrine aligns the four recovered fragments.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.brief.c202b9478b64": "Return to the formation and fire one close scanner pulse while the Drift archive records all seventeen hull counts.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.brief.f90d6d2475db": "Sit inside the sweep and fire one close scanner pulse so the recorder catches a full eight-second cycle from under the beam.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.successtext.144d66eefc5a": "Provenance filed. Three plate walls resolved to hull registries; the broker paid without asking which story got more expensive.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.successtext.21584100cc4b": "Window filed. The Fence paid the moment the file confirmed the beam does not keep perfect time.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.successtext.a3d5f6283714": "The four fragments resolve into one unfinished phrase. The Echo Shrine files your reconstruction and the Vael answer with payment, not explanation.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.successtext.db346cee721a": "Census filed. Seventeen counts agree on nothing except the formation; the archive pays for the record and asks no questions.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.successtext.db8a0dae0d49": "Reading filed. The post logged the street that lit as an equipment anomaly; the record says otherwise.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.successtext.e2ae1d97ccf2": "Survey filed. The pattern remains at Veil as a field record, not a claim.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.successtext.fc91bd307b5e": "Return frame filed. The probe brought back one image and no telemetry; the shaft remains unexplained.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.summary.11d9148a8a9a": "Seventeen hulls, seventeen living-crew counts, no two alike. Drift Market pays for the full filed record, not an explanation.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.summary.33be7afdb51a": "Research Station Veil will file one clean field record, not a salvage claim. Take the required close reading, or stay for extra pulses that bring the Vael watch forward.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.summary.531c57be04bd": "Four remembered notes now agree on the shape of the Vael schism. Trusted pilots may let the shrine play them as one sequence.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.summary.5beaafea252f": "Every wall of the Throne was once somebody else's hull, and the Bazaar sells those stories by the plate. The broker pays for a registry read done at the wall, not one invented on the berth.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.summary.635662a0f097": "Navigators calibrate to the Metronome; the Fence sells the gap between its returns. Margin pays for one cycle timed from inside the sweep, not for a copy of the shipping schedules it already keeps.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.summary.a281020f4c49": "The dead rivers and the cycling city lights have outlived their star, and the Directorate's rim post wants to know what still answers. One clean field record, taken from inside the arc, filed correctly.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.summary.e23b7c5bcd67": "Ordinary probes come back blank. The Cut refinery has one hardened shell and wants the exact return filed, even if it is only a frame.",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.title.0ad966afa802": "The Metronome: Off-Beat Window",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.title.394b92defc9c": "C13d-2 · Trophy Provenance Ledger",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.title.45345bd0e4f3": "The Resonance Obelisk: Quiet Survey",
  "loc.src.data.landmarkmissions.field.title.4554f5024dcd": "The Skerris Throne: Trophy Provenance",
